    "semantics": "Logistic regression of fall (case 1, control 0; other values left out) on galiamelo_apr2, adjusted for age_group7 and sex, each entered as categories against the first value in sorted order. Fitted by maximum likelihood (IRLS). Wald: coefficient plus or minus z times the standard error from the inverse information. Likelihood-ratio (profile): each limit is where the log-likelihood, refitted with that coefficient held fixed, has fallen by z^2/2 from its maximum. z for 95% is 1.959963984540054. A row missing any of the four columns is left out.",
    "equivalentTo": "statsmodels: smf.glm('y ~ C(galiamelo_apr2) + C(age_group7) + C(sex)', family=Binomial()).fit(); R: glm(..., family = binomial) with confint() for the profile limits.",
